3. Responsibilities
-------------------

3.1. Distribution of Source Form with Modifications

If You distribute Covered Software in Source Code Form that contains
Modifications made by You, You must:
(a) identify the portions of the Covered Software that contain Your
    Modifications;
(b) disclose, display, or otherwise make available the source code of
    those Modifications under the license grant of Section 2.1(a), with
    the notice described in Section 2.5.1, to anyone who is in receipt of
    the Covered Software; and
(c) if the Covered Software in Source Code Form does not already include
    a notice in the form described in Section 2.5.1, include a reasonable
    notice in the files that contain Your Modifications, or in a notice
    file required for Covered Software.

3.2. Distribution of Executable Form

If You distribute Covered Software in Executable Form then:
(a) such Covered Software must also be made available in Source Code
    Form, and You must inform recipients of the Executable Form how they
    can obtain a copy of such Source Code Form by reasonable means in a
    timely manner, at a charge no more than the cost of distribution to
    the recipient; and
(b) You may distribute such Executable Form under the terms of this
    License, or sublicense it under different terms, provided that the
    license for the Executable Form does not attempt to limit or alter
    the recipient's rights in the Source Code Form under this License.

3.3. Distribution of Larger Works

You may create a Larger Work by combining Covered Software with other
code not governed by the terms of this License and distribute the Larger
Work as a single product. In such a case, You must ensure that the
requirements of this License are fulfilled for the Covered Software,
including the portion of the Larger Work that constitutes Covered
Software.

4. Inability to Comply Due to Statute or Regulation
---------------------------------------------------

If it is impossible for You to comply with any of the terms of this
License with respect to some or all of the Covered Software due to
statute, judicial order, or regulation, then You must: (a) comply with
the terms of this License to the maximum extent possible; and (b)
describe the limitations and the code they affect. Such description must
be placed in a text file that is included with all distributions of the
Covered Software under this License. Except to the extent prohibited by
statute or regulation, such description must be sufficiently detailed for
a recipient of ordinary skill to be able to understand it.

5. Termination
--------------

5.1. The rights granted under this License will terminate automatically if
You fail to comply with any of its terms. However, if You become compliant,
then the rights granted under this License from a particular Contributor
are reinstated (a) provisionally, unless and until such Contributor
explicitly and finally terminates Your grants, and (b) on an ongoing basis,
if such Contributor fails to notify You of the non-compliance by some
reasonable means prior to 60 days after You have come back into compliance.
Moreover, Your grants from a particular Contributor are reinstated on an
ongoing basis if such Contributor notifies You of the non-compliance by
some reasonable means, this is the first time You have received notice of
non-compliance with these License terms from such Contributor, and You
become compliant prior to 30 days after Your receipt of the notice.

5.2. If You initiate litigation against any entity by asserting a patent
infringement claim (excluding declaratory judgment actions, counter-claims,
and cross-claims) alleging that a Contributor Version infringes Your
patents, then the rights granted to You by that Contributor under
Section 2.1(b) shall terminate on the date such litigation is filed.

